    <item>
      <title>HS Wrestling Wrap: Hopewell Valley ends dual CVC dual meet season with win over Lawrence</title>
      <link>https://www.trentonian.com/2026/02/03/hs-wrestling-wrap-hopewell-valley-ends-dual-cvc-dual-meet-season-with-win-over-lawrence/</link>
      <description>Led by a pin by Scott Mangan at 190 pounds, the Hopewell Valley wrestling team crushed Lawrence, 63-17, Tuesday night. Mangan lost by the score of 14-11 to Lawrence’s James Lyons in the finals of the CVC Championships on Saturday, but it was a different story on Tuesday as he pinned Lyons in 3:03. Hopewell also got pins in the first period from Jan Rahmani (106), Parker Humphrey (126), Max Pollara (157) and Ethan Barker (175). Steven Ham remained undefeated for Lawrence with a pin at 132 pounds.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.trentonian.com/2026/02/03/hs-wrestling-wrap-hopewell-valley-ends-dual-cvc-dual-meet-season-with-win-over-lawrence/</guid>
